          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "accordion_IigYyX": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "name": "t:names.accordion",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "plus",
            "dividers": true,
            "divider_color": "",
            "type_preset": "",
            "background_color": "",
            "text_color": "",
            "border": "none",
            "border_width": 1,
            "border_opacity": 100,
            "border_color": "",
            "border_radius": 0,
            "padding-block-start": 0,
            "padding-block-end": 0,
            "padding-inline-start": 0,
            "padding-inline-end": 0
          },
          "blocks": {
            "accordion_row_hlTMpz": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How easy it to set up the Giant Grill Gauge?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_RJgdLC": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p><a href=\"https://combustion.inc/pages/setup-guide/giant-grill-gauge\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://combustion.inc/pages/setup-guide/giant-grill-gauge\">Setup is straightforward.</a> Attach  the mount to your grill where your old gauge was, then secure it with the wingnut. </p><p>The Giant Grill Gauge display snaps onto the mount magnetically. Once attached, all you have to do is turn it on.</p><p>Connect it to your Wi-Fi network easily using the Combustion app.</p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_RJgdLC"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_FvkSbJ": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Will the Giant Grill Gauge fit my grill?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_OXdIby": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>The Giant Grill Gauge is compatible with most grills and smokers, including popular brands like Big Green Egg, Traeger, Weber, and more. </p><p><strong>Will it work with mine?</strong></p><ul><li>You'll need a clear, circular area of 4.5\" (11.5cm) diameter where the display can sit (not \"hanging off\" an edge)</li><li>You'll need a pass-through hole for the sensor tube; this hole will need to be minimum 5/32\" up to 1/4\" (4-6mm)</li><li>The sensor tube diameter is 3.8mm</li><li>The small gap between the sensor tube and the lid will be covered by the spring clip, allowing only minimal smoke loss</li></ul><p>In some cases, mounting the Giant Grill Gauge may require a hole to be drilled, or an adjustment to be made to an existing hole. </p><p>NOTE: we absolutely DO NOT recommend drilling a hole (or adjusting the size of the hole) on a ceramic grill. </p><p>Looking for a <a href=\"https://combustion.inc/pages/faq?hcUrl=%2Fen-US%2Fwill-it-fit-fitment-guide-for-giant-grill-gauge-and-combustion-engine-986118\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://combustion.inc/pages/faq?hcUrl=%2Fen-US%2Fwill-it-fit-fitment-guide-for-giant-grill-gauge-and-combustion-engine-986118\">printable template to check the fit on your grill? </a>It's on the help center.</p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_OXdIby"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_vdmwMk": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Is there any reason NOT to get the thicker Heat Shield except for the higher price?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_gzxeAp": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>This question has come up a lot, so here goes:</p><p>No. </p><p><strong>The Heat Shield variant is universal </strong>(for anything that can hold a Giant Grill Gauge). </p><p>Sometimes it’s overkill. (Some people like that.)</p><p>Use Heat Shield:</p><ul><li>With a Weber Kettle</li><li>Or any kettle-style grill</li><li>For a top-mount </li><li>If you’re really into pushing things hotter (pizza cooks, this is you!). </li><li><strong>When in doubt </strong></li></ul><p>That said, the Deflector will work with many (most?) grills and smokers. It’s still very robust (up to 600ºF lid temps). </p><p>Use Heat Deflector for: </p><ul><li>Replacing front-mounted gauges</li><li>Insulated grills and smokers</li><li>Gas grills</li><li>Most kamado-style grills</li><li>Improved aerodynamics</li></ul><p>We are compiling a master list with more specific recommendations, so if you have a specific grill in mind, please write in <a href=\"mailto:hello@combustion.inc\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">hello@combustion.inc</span></a>.</p><p>If we already have a recommendation, we’ll tell you. Either way, we’ll add it to the list.</p><p>(P.S. Please help us out by putting GGG as part of the subject line of that email.) </p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_gzxeAp"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_qNquiO": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Can I make changes to my order?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_SadFNv": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes - you can make changes or cancel your order at any time before it ships – at no cost. </p><p>A lot of people are unsure about the choice of mount - that’s understandable. </p><p>There are a lot of different grills out there! We’re mapping it out as requests come in (don’t be shy- <a href=\"mailto:support@combustion.inc\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Combustion customer support\">email us</a> with your particulars, and of course photos are appreciated). </p><p>Don’t sweat it, you’ll have an opportunity to revise your choice before shipping. </p><p><strong>For now, we recommend you choose Heat Shield if you’re unsure.</strong></p><p>There will be more details forthcoming about what mount is ideal for particular grills. </p><p>And we will likely produce some affordable adapter kits to manage nonstandard mounts. Stay tuned! </p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_SadFNv"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_tUCSwE": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What's included?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_jeFtUH": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Includes: </p><p>• Giant Grill Gauge display</p><p>• Heat Shield or Heat Deflector mount</p><p>• Sensor tube (with M4 threading)</p><p>• 1/4-20 threaded mounting tube with washer and wingnut</p><p>• M4 wing nut and washer</p><p>• 2 CR2450 batteries (85 °C rated)</p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_jeFtUH"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_tdYjtW": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Does it work as part of the mesh network? Specifically, will it help get the signal from my CPT out of the grill box better?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_IsOdQW": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes! It’s part of the Bluetooth mesh network (Meatnet™) and also adds WiFi to your toolset.</p><p>The Giant Grill Gauge connects to Meatnet and communicates with other Combustion tools, but also connects directly to your Wi-Fi network. This gives you the ability to remotely check temps using the app – from far beyond Bluetooth range. </p><p><strong>From the CPT’s point of view, it’s creating a direct line-of-sight Bluetooth connection inside the grill!</strong> </p><p>The signal coming from the CPT doesn’t have to penetrate the box, it has a backdoor. And then the Gauge passes that on to whatever else you’ve got - Boosters, Displays, Apps. And so forth.</p><p>That also means the Gauge is not dependent on WiFi - you can still use it as a repeater with traditional Meatnet, even if the internet goes down. </p><p>On top of this, the Gauge is contributing its own data (grill temp) to the pool, which creates all kinds of interesting and useful analytical possibilities. Mathematical!</p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_IsOdQW"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_dxBpBi": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Can it handle multiple Predictive Thermometers?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_lgqGho": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>The Giant Grill Gauge can <strong>manage up to 4 Predictive Thermometers </strong>simultaneously. </p><p>It connects to them via Bluetooth and then extends their range using its WiFi connection. </p><p>This allows you to view data from all connected thermometers from anywhere with an internet connection.</p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_lgqGho"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_BRhbik": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Will it have high/low temp alarms? Like for flame-outs or flare-ups, or whatever?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_qosxCM": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes! Custom alarms are included in the Combustion App.<br/><br/>Set high or low alarms in the Combustion Inc App. If your cook goes over temp (or under), you'll get alerts from your phone as well as audible alarms and visual alerts on the Gauge itself. No worries!</p><p>You can also set these custom alarms on your Combustion Predictive Thermometer.</p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_qosxCM"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_DOVmYO": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Is it weather-resistant?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_BaEwYk": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yup, it's fully weather resistant. </p><p>We've also put a bunch of UV protection into the silicone housing and coating on the LCD display. <strong>But sunlight is brutal. </strong></p><p>Highly recommended you just pop it off the magnetic mount and store it on your refrigerator when it's not in use. It will stay looking brand-new for a lot longer.</p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_BaEwYk"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_LlGwhk": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Will there be a blower for temperature control in the future?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_dSGkQK": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>That's a popular question! We're always cooking up new ideas.</p><p>EDIT: Here it is, by popular request: the <a href=\"/products/combustion-engine\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Combustion Engine\">Combustion Engine wireless blower</a>.</p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_dSGkQK"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_NyOPqx": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Why isn't the Giant Grill Gauge available in black?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_rCiHYm": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Heat management. Black absorbs more heat, while lighter colors stay cooler. Think of it like wearing a t-shirt on a hot, sunny day. </p><p>Our Combustion yellow helps keep the gauge from overheating in direct sunlight, ensuring reliable performance. </p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_rCiHYm"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_EBoyoP": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Why aren't the batteries rechargeable?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_BGzYDL": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>The Giant Grill Gauge is designed for extreme outdoor conditions. </p><p>Rechargeable lithium polymer batteries can be compromised at temperatures above 149°F (65°C), which the Gauge may exceed on very hot, sunny days. </p><p>Because of that we use high-capacity coin cell batteries that can withstand extreme temperatures while providing enough power for most customers to change batteries only once every year or two. This ensures reliability in all grilling conditions without sacrificing performance or convenience.</p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_BGzYDL"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_xjhrzA": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What is warranty and customer support like?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 12
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_vDKNGw": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>We stand behind our products with a 2-year warranty. </p><p><a href=\"/pages/warranty\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Warranty\">Warranty details here</a>.</p><p>Our full-time support team is always ready to help. </p><p>But don't be surprised if you hear from our designers, engineers, or even our founder Chris. We're all passionate about our products and eager to help you get the most out of them.</p><p>There'll for sure be ample discussion about the Giant Grill Gauge on our <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/combustion_inc/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/combustion_inc/\">subreddit.</a></p><p></p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
